  "scope": "Task `3a0af56db83e`; production generator SHA-256 `773d54bdbec469ca64c9e2037e2a9cf1ef0033aa601e4539c482b0332d7ee4f1`; prototype-only repair.\nDefect \u2192 repair: hidden seed parity controlled public creation order \u2192 public artifacts are now planned and written by visible-content filename order.\nThe production generator, canonical data, selected Racket authority, and `RULE_HASH=d5832237956b` are unchanged.\nTest-first regression: old seed-0 writer failed (`6ff\u2026` before `1e\u2026`); repaired writer passed.\nFocused parametric suite: 18/18 passed (`checks/parametric-focused-tests-final.log`).\nPacket source-bound task suite: 57/57 passed (`checks/task-tests-final/result.json`).\nFresh Racket evidence: 7/7 canonical labels and 12/12 episode labels; 2 settings, 4 demos, 8 queries, 0 ambiguities.\nAdversarial check: seeds 0\u20133 emitted sorted public batches, duplicate visible IDs were rejected before public emission, public views exposed no private fields, and a tampered artifact was rejected.\nRemaining limit: raw direct task-directory collection cannot import the packet-omitted generated `puzzle_generators.per_puzzle` package; the supported staged wrapper is green.\nTickets: the pinned historical singleton audit reproduced exactly; a current-source rarest-palette shortcut was refuted by one lawful Racket-backed witness with no safety finding.\nAssessment: routine narrow privacy repair; the `lower_band_order` prototype remains unapproved and outside production/training admission.\nNext useful promotion step: use the shared public-challenge byte/ID helper rather than maintaining a task-local equivalent.",
